        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://vermont.com/cities/irasburg/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Caleb Leach became the first settler of Irasburg in 1798, though the land had been granted years earlier.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irasburg%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Irasburg served as the Orleans County shire town from 1812 until 1886.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irasburg%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The production of salts and pearl-ashes was the primary industry in Irasburg during the early nineteenth century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irasburg%2C_Vermont"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "By the 1820s, Irasburg prospered with industrial sites including a woolen mill, a tannery, and factories producing stoves and plows.",
